00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:09,560
small market changes in supplier demand, you will for

420
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:12,640
large changes.

421
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:15,640
The idea is that for a small change, then you'll say, well,

422
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:19,040
the amount of surplus or shortage is so small, we're

423
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:22,480
only losing a little bit of money, and that money is

424
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:24,840
smaller than the menu costs.

